This extension adds Deus Ex modding support to Vortex Mod Manager.
[summary]Deus Exe launcher installed automatically.[/summary]

[size=3][b]This extension will automatically download and install the [url=https://kentie.net/article/dxguide/index.htm]Deus Exe Launcher[/url]. This is required to improve game compatibility with modern systems.[/b][/size]

[b]✅ Supported Versions:[/b]
[list]
[*]Steam[/*]
[*]GOG[/*]
[*]Other versions may need to select the installation location manually.[/*]
[/list]
[b]🛠️ Mod Installation Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]Mod Folder mods with a "Community Update" folder install to the game folder.[/*]
[*]Root Folder mods with a "System" folder install to the game folder.[/*]
[*]Deus Exe (Launcher) mods with a "deusex.exe" file install to the "System" folder.[/*]
[*]Binaries (Engine Injector) mods with an "engine.dll", "deusexechelonrenderer.dll", "d3d9.dll" or "rtx.conf" file and a ".exe", ".dll", ".asi" or ".addon64" file install to the "System" folder.[/*]
[*]Archives with a FOMOD installer (a "fomod" folder with ModuleConfig.xml) are handed to Vortex's built-in FOMOD installer instead.[/*]
[/list]
[b]📋 Usage Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]You can open several useful files/folders/URLs using the buttons within the folder icon on the Mods toolbar.[/*]
[*]Automatically downloads and installs Deus Exe launcher to the "System" (binaries) folder.[/*]
[*]Installs select mods directly to the "System" folder (i.e. d3d9.dll, engine.dll, etc.).[/*]
[/list]

[b]📝 Notes for Mod Authors:[/b]
[spoiler]
Packaging rules for Deus Ex mods, so Vortex installs them to the right place.

Vortex decides what a mod is by looking at the files and folders inside the archive. It tries each installer in order and the first one that matches wins, so archive layout is what determines where your mod ends up.

========================================================================

Mod Folder:

Recognised when the archive contains a "Community Update" folder.

  Installs to: the game folder

========================================================================

Root / Game Folder Mods:

For mods laid out the same way the files appear inside the game folder. Vortex copies the matched folder and everything under it straight into the game.

[code]
MyRootMod.zip
└── System\
    └── ... files in their real relative locations
[/code]

  Requirements:
    - Recognised by a folder named "System", "Maps", "Textures", "Sounds", "Music", "Save" or "GOTY_1" in the archive.

  Installs to: the game folder

  Common mistakes:
    - Zipping the folder that CONTAINS the game folders, instead of the game folders themselves, adds an extra level and misplaces every file.

========================================================================

Deus Exe (Launcher):

Recognised when the archive contains a "deusex.exe" file.

  Installs to: "System"

========================================================================

Binaries (Engine Injector):

Recognised when the archive contains a "engine.dll", "deusexechelonrenderer.dll", "d3d9.dll" or "rtx.conf" file and a ".exe", ".dll", ".asi" or ".addon64" file.

  Installs to: "System"

========================================================================

Rules That Apply To Every Mod Type:

    - Archives that contain a FOMOD installer (a "fomod" folder with "ModuleConfig.xml") are handed to Vortex's built-in FOMOD installer instead, and none of the rules above apply.
    - Folder and file name matching is case-insensitive.
    - Extra wrapper folders around a recognised folder are generally fine; the installer searches at any depth.
[/spoiler]

